>>> read ok {"path":"package.json"}
{
  "name": "report-tool",
  "type": "commonjs",
  "dependencies": {
    "chalk": "^5.3.0"
  }
}
>>> bash ok {"command":"grep -rn \"require(\\\"chalk\\\")\" src"}
src/print.js:1:const chalk = require("chalk");
>>> final
`ERR_REQUIRE_ESM` means CommonJS code called `require()` on a package that is ESM-only. Here, src/print.js does `require("chalk")`, and chalk 5 ships only as an ES module, while your package is `"type": "commonjs"`. Either pin chalk to 4.x, which still supports `require`, or load it with `await import("chalk")` (or move the project to ESM).
